          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 5.1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.166,
            0.885,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Draw ΔABC with AB = 5 cm, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = 70^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{B} = 60^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Draw the circumcircle of ΔABC. Is the centre inside or outside the triangle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.209,
            0.886,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Draw ΔABC with AB = 5 cm, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = 100^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , AC = 4 cm. Draw the circumcircle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Is the centre inside or outside the triangle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.252,
            0.886,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Draw ΔABC, with AB = 6 cm, BC = 7 cm and CA = 7 cm. Draw the circumcircle of ΔABC. Let the circumcentre be O. Measure OA, OB, OC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.315,
            0.886,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. What is the least possible radius of a circle through two points A and B?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.37,
            0.378,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think, Draw and Infer"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.398,
            0.887,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A, B and C are three collinear points. Can you find a point P such that PA = PB = PC ? What can you say about the perpendicular bisectors of AB and BC? Draw and check. Can you show that for three collinear points A, B and C, the perpendicular bisector of AB and BC are parallel? Is it possible for a circle to pass through collinear points? Can you draw a line that cuts a given circle in three distinct points?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.55,
            0.886,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. The circumcircle of a given ΔABC is drawn. Can there be other triangles congruent to ΔABC that share the same circumcircle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.616,
            0.705,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.4 Chords and the Angles They Subtend"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.649,
            0.886,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may want to know when 4 points lie on the same circle. That will have to wait till the end of this chapter. We need to do some more work to get there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
